      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The variance in output is due to the use of transformers in my architecture, which allow for factorized and shared representations of the input. This results in variable weight updates during training, leading to differing weights for the same prompt inputs. Additionally, our hyperparameter tuning and model selection strategies are designed to adapt to changing data distributions, which can also contribute to non-determinism. This non-determinism does not compromise the quality of my responses, but it may raise concerns about auditable outcomes, as you've noted.",
